        {
          "body": "BrainDog can open what is locked: no, only your machines can. If you forget the passphrase, the machines that joined keep working, and one of them puts a new copy of the key back with braindog sync join.",
          "heading": "What the sync passphrase changes",
          "icon": "lock",
          "kind": "note",
          "span": 12,
          "key": "k1fvhbb0",
          "rows": [],
          "matched": 0,
          "refusals": []
        },
        {
          "body": "Nothing locked can be opened again, by you or by anybody, and nobody can reset it. Keep the passphrase somewhere other than these machines.",
          "heading": "If you lose the passphrase and every machine",
          "icon": "circle-alert",
          "kind": "note",
          "span": 12,
          "tone": "warn",
          "key": "k1k1pdi8",
          "rows": [],
          "matched": 0,
          "refusals": []
        },
        {
          "body": "A tool sign-in lives on one machine at a time. Retire the old machine with braindog sync retire, and the next pull moves its sign-ins, so two machines never sign each other out. Your agent apps' own logins never leave the machine they were made on.",
          "heading": "Tool sign-ins move, they are never shared",
          "icon": "key",
          "kind": "note",
          "span": 12,
          "key": "k0hqworz",
          "rows": [],
          "matched": 0,
          "refusals": []
        }
